          <li><strong>Automated Abuse &amp; Scraping:</strong> Deploying automated spiders, scrapers, bots, or scripts to flood our servers with mass extraction requests or overwhelm system bandwidth.</li>
          <li><strong>Circumvention of Security:</strong> Attempting to bypass, disable, or tamper with Digital Rights Management (DRM) technologies, paywalls, access tokens, or technical protection measures.</li>
          <li><strong>Malicious Activities:</strong> Transmitting malware, viruses, injection scripts, or attempting to reverse-engineer our serverless backend architecture.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

